Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec,comp.unix.osf.osf1,comp.unix.osf.misc


Hello all.

I have a problem. I'm trying to create a dial-in PPP server on DEC Alpha
running Digital UNIX 3.2G. I can't get the modem to talk to Alpha. Let
me explain.

First, I took my experimental DEC Alpha 200 running Digital UNIX 4.0A
and set the modem and the machine as Dial-in PPP server *properly*. I
was using guidelines from "Setting up PPP server - Network
Administration" for DU4.0. Now, when I tried to transfer that solution
to our DEC Alpha 4100 server running Digital UNIX 3.2G, Alpha couldn't
talk to modem.

When I tried to use "tip" utility to talk to modem, all I got were
characters that looked like a circle with a slash. There was no response
to AT or any other command.

The next odd thing were LEDs on the modem. Normally, when modem is not
connected to Alpha or Alpha isn't using it (no getty in respawn mode),
the only LEDs lit are AA (AutoAnswer) and CS (Clear to Send). And when I
start "tip" or activate getty, DT (Data Terminal ready) also lits up.
But when I connect the modem to 4100, all THREE are lit instantly. Like
4100 is using COM port all the time.

I have tried connecting modem to several machines, some running DU4.0,
others OSF/1 3.2. All machines are doing OK, except our DEC Alpha 4100.
On the other hand, I couldn't find any proces using COM1 (/dev/tty00)
port. The only thing different on 4100 is an APC Smart UPS 3000,
connected to COM2 (/dev/tty01), using smart signaling (COULD THIS BE A
PROBLEM?)

Here is my configuration.

Machine: DEC Alpha 4100 server
         1 CPU 300 MHz
         512 MB RAM
         RAID 5 + 1, 16 GB drive
         Ethernet 10 Mbit
         2 serial + 1 paralel + 1 terminal port(?)

Modem:   US Robotics Sportser 33.6 - external

OS:      Digital UNIX 3.2G

UPS:     APC Smart 3000
         Smart signaling on COM2 (/dev/tty01)
         APC PowerCHUTE monitoring software
          *** COULD THIS BE THE CAUSE? ***

USR modem was set, as explained in PPP server setup docs. The setting
took place on my DEC Alpha 200, where I tested the first PPP dial-in
server. The settings were:

AT &C1  - Normal CD operation
   &D2  - Normal DTR operation
   Q1   - Quiet mode
   E0   - No local echo
   S0=2 - Autoanswer after 2 rings
   &W0  - Write this to NVRAM(0)

Could smart signaling from APC UPS be the cause of my problems or is it
something else?

TYIA,
Nix.

P.S. If you could also E-Mail answers to nikola@ev.ns.ac.yu, I would be
grateful.




