Well, there have been some new developments. First of all, I have
established partial communication with modem, but I=9Em still stuck.

LEDs are unchanged.

The reason I couldn=9Et communicate with modem, using "tip", was the baud=

rate of COM port. IT WON'T WORK AT 38400! When I set it to 9600, I
finally got response from modem:

AT

OK

AT&D2&C1S0=3D2

OK

ATQ1E0&W0

At that moment I was convinced that the communication will go, after
all. There was still some unpleasent feeling in the back of my head
about those LEDs. And I was right.

PC with USR Sportser 33.6 and LAN WorkPlace Pro: PPP support, Dialer and
Host Presenter was used as a client. Dialing goes OK, modems talk to
each other and establish connection: 9600/ARQ/V32/V42bis.

And then NO RESPONCE FROM ALPHA! I tried HyperTerminal, anything, the
Alpha is not responding, the /usr/sbin/getty just sits there on
/dev/tty00. Nothing.

Then I killed off getty from inittab, established connection from PC to
Alpha's modem. Then I sent a string like this:

echo "Hello" > /dev/tty00

The string appeared on the PC's terminal screen.

So, to summarize.

PC           --> Modem(PC)    =3D=3D OK
Modem(PC)    --> Modem(ALPHA) =3D=3D OK
Modem(Alpha) --> Alpha        =3D=3D NOT OK !!!!!!!!!!!!

Alpha        --> Modem(Alpha) =3D=3D OK
Modem(Alpha) --> Modem(PC)    =3D=3D OK
Modem(PC)    --> PC           =3D=3D OK

Does anybody have any ideas?
I'm starting to suspect console firmware, I think I saw 9600 somewhere
among those variables.

TYIA,
Nix.





