Nikola Milutinovic wrote:
> =

> Well, there have been some new developments. First of all, I have
> established partial communication with modem, but I=9Em still stuck.
> =

> LEDs are unchanged.

[SNIP]

> Does anybody have any ideas?
> I'm starting to suspect console firmware, I think I saw 9600 somewhere
> among those variables.

I tried the whole thing with null-modem cable and a PC (no modems). Set
getty to use direct line, no modem controll and it worked!!! Then I
tried the whole thing with modems, but used non-modem setting for getty,
after the modems negotiated connection. It worked again. When I try
getty without modem support, before modems do their stuff, getty kills
AutoAnswer on modem >:-(.

Well, the problem was "solved". In the firmware console I ran into this:

com1_baud	9600
com1_flow	SOFTWARE
com1_modem	OFF

So I tried to change speed to 38400 and modem support to ON. Console
accepted modem change, but it didn't reflect itself on LEDs (first bad
sign!). Speed setting was rejected, saying that "for non-default speed
values Serial ROM had to be changed" (second bad sign!).

The behavior of the Alpha DIDN'T change at all (LEDs and getty). So
bottom line is that DEC Alpha 4100 has castrated COM ports and doesn't
support modems.

I must say, I'm displeased. That Alpha cost us $80,000. They could have
given us proper COM ports.

Nix.




