Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec,comp.unix.osf.misc,comp.unix.osf.osf1


Hello!

We are using an digital alphaserver 4100 with 2 GB RAM and 4 CPUs and
OSF1/Digital Unix V4.0. We are running apache V1.2 and are experiencing
serious problems under heavy load. It appears that most of the active
server-processes hang in the "w" (sending reply) status, and no new
connections are accepted. "/usr/sbin/netstat -a -f inet -n" reports many
sockets in the TIME_WAIT or FIN_WAIT_n, where n = 1,2, status (more than
60%). In this situation our customers report a very slow system
response.

Do you know if this behavior stands in any relation to the more often
experienced TIME_WAIT and FIN_WAIT_n status of the sockets? And if yes,
is there any kernel parameter, which forces the tcp-module to close the
connections?

Thanks in advance,
  Eric Heymann



